# Skelica — Frontend Environment Variables
#
# Copy to frontend/.env and fill in what you need. Vite only exposes variables
# prefixed with VITE_ to the browser, so only ever put non-secret values here.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Funnel analytics (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Without a provider configured, every track() call is a console.debug no-op and
# nothing is ever sent. Events never include prompt content — only lengths,
# scores, grades and component counts.
#
# Option A — Plausible (cookieless, custom events):
# VITE_ANALYTICS_PROVIDER=plausible
# VITE_ANALYTICS_DOMAIN=skelica.pages.dev
#
# Option B — Umami (self-hostable, cookieless, custom events):
# VITE_ANALYTICS_PROVIDER=umami
# VITE_ANALYTICS_SCRIPT_URL=https://your-umami-host/script.js
# VITE_ANALYTICS_WEBSITE_ID=xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LLM keys
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE: the browser-side LLM optimizer is NOT wired into the UI. These keys are
# not read by the running app today.
#
# Do NOT put provider keys in a VITE_-prefixed variable — anything VITE_-prefixed
# is embedded in the shipped JavaScript and is public. Server-side keys belong in
# Cloudflare Workers secrets once the credits/optimization backend exists.
#
# The in-app Settings panel stores user-supplied keys in localStorage only.
